From 07cd915a1d1a194deafd05cdf2403e1e812f4a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:44:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wlcsm: take ASUS 40585's libnvram.so / libwlcsm.so pair for
 the RT-BE96U

The 42015 pair Reaper carried since v3.1.8 (the netlink socket-leak fix) is
superseded by the pair in the 102_40585 GPL, which every BE model in the
new base already ships. Measured 2026-10-27: libwlcsm is the same code
(layout only); libnvram is the same code plus a caller check in
nvram_set(): only init, rc, httpd(s), cfg_server/cfg_client, asd, ahs and
ookla_quota_mon may write sshd_enable, sshd_port, sshd_pass,
sshd_authkeys or ookla_quota. Every Reaper writer of those keys is httpd
or rc. A shell `nvram set` of one of them is now refused (returns -1,
logged only at debug level).

Both files move together (libwlcsm imports wlcsm_agent, whose layout the
pair shares).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../wlan/nvram/prebuilt/libnvram.so           | Bin 35916 -> 44716 bytes
 .../wlcsm/prebuilt/libwlcsm.so                | Bin 46708 -> 56368 bytes
 2 files changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/router-sysdep.rt-be96u/wlan/nvram/prebuilt/libnvram.so b/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/router-sysdep.rt-be96u/wlan/nvram/prebuilt/libnvram.so
